  "notes": "Two distinct failure modes modeled: the original design/restraint failure (root cause, chain origin, CAUSED_BY cause node) and the troubleshooting process deficiency from the Nov 2022 precursor event, which is linked upstream via LEADS_TO to the restraint failure since it explains why the underlying condition was not corrected before the Feb 2023 recurrence. No previous similar occurrence LER was cited (narrative explicitly states none in the last three years with same/similar cause), so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge was created despite mention of the Nov 4, 2022 internal precursor (which is not a separate LER). Redundant onsite power is mentioned only in a safety-assessment context ('no loss of safety function occurred... based on availability of redundant onsite power') without naming a specific operable system during the inoperability window, so per Rule 6 no BACKED_UP_BY edge/System node was created for it."
